Social media platforms like Facebook and WhatsApp allow users to stay in touch with loved ones across the globe, bridging geographical gaps effectively.
Real-time communication features such as video calls and messaging enable instant interaction, fostering a sense of closeness despite physical separation.
Social media connects people with similar interests and communities, creating global networks that enhance cultural exchange and understanding.
During crises, social media has been instrumental in coordinating relief efforts and sharing critical information, demonstrating its role in global communication.
The ability to maintain and build relationships through social media has been shown to reduce feelings of isolation and loneliness in many users.